Logical: KGImplementationPractice
Title: "Knowledge graph L1-LIBRARY: Implementation practice"
Description: "A statement of how to put guidance into practice, printed in a publication whose publicationType is implementation-guidance or methodology: the handbook's \"products that are not guidelines\" (§1.9), a \"how to\" document that makes no recommendations of its own. Not a recommendation, and not a good practice statement — both are made by a guideline and approved by the GRC; this is neither. It carries no kind, direction, strength or certainty, because nothing graded it. A handbook's own \"Best practices\" lists are the typical source. Owner ruling 1b, 2026-10-12: model these as their own class, not as recommendation nodes of a new kind. statement is verbatim and is the only stored copy, as recommendation's is. identifier is used in the IRI. There is no remark: L1 3.0's remark is minted under a recommendation (its iriPattern) and hasRemark starts at one, so a remark of a practice needs L1 itself to change — proposed upstream, not patched here. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/implementation-practice."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* identifier 0..1 string "Identifier" "The key the extraction gives it (e.g. NPC-R06), or the printed number where the publication numbers its practices; used in the IRI."
* statement 0..1 markdown "Statement" "The practice, VERBATIM; the only stored copy."
* contentHash 0..1 string "Content hash" "sha256 of the normalised statement; unchanged on re-extraction means current."

Logical: KGLibraryNode
Title: "Knowledge graph L1-LIBRARY: Library node"
Description: "A node in the ingested library L1 is read from: a source document, a section or a block, addressed by the library's own IRI. Opaque, as L1 asserts nothing about the library's internal model; the library is upstream, so pointing at it keeps the layering rule. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/library-node."

* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"
* iri 0..1 uri "IRI" "The library node's own IRI."
* libraryClass 0..1 uri "Library class" "The library class it is an instance of (cat-harness:SourceDocument, doco:Section, cat-harness:Block, …)."
* entry 0..1 string "Entry" "The library entry it belongs to (e.g. 9789240016514-eng)."
* pageRange 0..1 string "Page range" "Physical pages it covers, where it is a section or block."
